<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW 2026-08-21. THE "AN APPROVAL IS PENDING" UI FLAG. SYSTEM-WRITTEN ONLY.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 A SECOND, DISTINCT FIELD FROM Approval_Advance_Pending__c. DO NOT CONFLATE THEM.
        =====================================================================================
        The two names differ by one word and they are opposites in time. Read this table before
        wiring anything to either of them:

            THIS FIELD (Approval_Pending__c)
              TRUE  while an approval is PENDING.
              Written ONLY by approval process actions: initialSubmissionActions sets it,
              and finalApprovalActions / finalRejectionActions / recallActions all clear it.
              Plus BovSubmissionTriggerHandler, which mirrors the BOV branch up from the child
              (see "THE FOURTH ACTION" below).
              Its lifetime is EXACTLY the ProcessInstance.Status = 'Pending' window.

            Approval_Advance_Pending__c
              The D-1 auto advance SEMAPHORE. Goes TRUE on FINAL APPROVAL, never on submission,
              and is cleared by DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable in the same DML that writes
              the new stage. It is deliberately LEFT TRUE when an advance is refused.
              Read that field's own XML comment before touching it.

        Precedent for carrying a banner like this rather than trusting the names to disambiguate
        themselves: BOV_Submission__c.Approval_Status__c versus Submission_Status__c, which are
        also two similarly named fields on one object with two different owners.

        =====================================================================================
        WHY THE FIELD EXISTS AT ALL
        =====================================================================================
        A FlexiPage visibility rule can read ONLY a field on the record itself. Every leftValue
        on Disposition_Record_Page is either {!Record.<FieldApiName>} or
        {!$Permission.CustomPermission.<Name>}; there is no approval state token, and approval
        state is not reachable by a formula either (no relationship from Disposition__c to
        ProcessInstance, and a formula cannot reach DOWN to the child BOV_Submission__c).
        So the fact has to be MATERIALISED as a stored field on the record. That is the same
        move this repo already made for the record type with Is_On_Market__c.

        =====================================================================================
        WHO READS IT: FOUR DYNAMIC ACTIONS, AND NOTHING ELSE
        =====================================================================================
        It is NOT on any page layout and NOT on any FlexiPage fieldInstance. Its only readers
        are these four actionNames visibility rules on Disposition_Record_Page, named here so
        the count stays checkable the way Is_On_Market__c's count is named in
        permissionsets/DPEG_Disposition_View.permissionset-meta.xml:
            Disposition__c.Submit_Sale_Decision
            Disposition__c.Submit_Selected_Broker
            Disposition__c.Submit_Broker_Selection
            Disposition__c.Submit_Closing_Approval
        Each rule ANDs {!Record.Approval_Pending__c} EQUAL false onto its EXISTING stage and
        Disposition_Deal_Actions criteria. Select_Offer is deliberately NOT one of them: it is
        a picker, not a submit button.

        🔴 UNLIKE Approval_Advance_Pending__c, THIS FIELD MUST HAVE READ FLS, AND THE POLARITY
        MAKES THAT LOAD BEARING. A visibility rule reading a field the running user cannot see
        evaluates FALSE with no error anywhere. With the EQUAL false polarity above, a missing
        grant does not fail safe: it hides ALL FOUR Submit buttons for EVERY user, silently and
        permanently. Read is granted in DPEG_Disposition_View and DPEG_Disposition_Edit and in
        no other set, mirroring Is_On_Market__c exactly. Those two files must land WITH OR
        BEFORE the FlexiPage, never after.
        It stays READ ONLY (editable=false) everywhere. Recovery from a stuck flag is anonymous
        Apex or Data Loader, not a hand edit.

        =====================================================================================
        THE FOURTH ACTION IS THE ODD ONE OUT
        =====================================================================================
        Three of the four approvals TARGET the Disposition, so their own field updates write
        this field directly. Submit_Selected_Broker's approval (Broker_Finalize_Approval)
        targets the child BOV_Submission__c instead, and BOV_Submission__c.Disposition__c is a
        LOOKUP, not Master Detail, which rules out both a roll up summary and a cross object
        workflow field update. That branch is therefore mirrored up by
        BovSubmissionTriggerHandler from BOV_Submission__c.Approval_Pending__c. Developer owned.

        =====================================================================================
        ⚠ WHY NO APEX WRITES THIS ON THE THREE DISPOSITION TARGET BRANCHES
        =====================================================================================
        All three set recordEditability = AdminOnly, so the Disposition is LOCKED for the whole
        pending window: any Apex write throws ENTITY_IS_LOCKED, and neither AccessLevel
        .SYSTEM_MODE nor a Queueable lifts a lock (a pending approval outlives the job). The
        approval process's own field update is the one writer that is not blocked, which is why
        this is declarative. An approval triggered FLOW was rejected for the reason recorded on
        Approval_Advance_Pending__c: with no runInMode it runs as the APPROVER and its DML hits
        the approver's read only access, a measured incident on this org.

        ⚠ TARGET SCOPING IS A PROPERTY OF THE CURRENT STAGE LAYOUT, NOT A GENERAL TRUTH. ONE
        flag serves all four actions only because the four entry stages are mutually exclusive
        (Disposition Readiness, BOV Outreach, Broker Selection, Closing) and each rule already
        ANDs its own stage. A FIFTH approval sharing one of those stages would make this flag
        hide the wrong button, silently. Same shape as the "ONE UPDATE SERVES ALL THREE
        APPROVALS" note in workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml.

        ⚠ NO VALIDATION RULE AND NO TRIGGER GUARD ENFORCE "DO NOT HAND EDIT". Read only FLS is
        the control. Do not add one; it was not requested.

        ⚠ DETECTION QUERY FOR A STUCK FLAG (a true with no pending approval behind it):
            SELECT Id, Name, Disposition_Stage__c FROM Disposition__c
            WHERE Approval_Pending__c = true
              AND Id NOT IN (SELECT TargetObjectId FROM ProcessInstance WHERE Status = 'Pending')

        DEPLOY ORDER, LOAD BEARING. This file must land BEFORE
        workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml (a field update naming a field that does not
        exist fails the deploy), which must itself land before the three approval processes.
    -->
    <fullName>Approval_Pending__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>false</defaultValue>
    <description>SYSTEM FIELD - DO NOT HAND-EDIT. TRUE while an approval is pending on this disposition. Set by the approval initialSubmissionActions and cleared by its final approval, final rejection and recall actions; the BOV branch is mirrored up by BovSubmissionTriggerHandler. Read ONLY by four Dynamic Actions on Disposition_Record_Page, which hide the matching Submit button while it is true. A SECOND, DISTINCT field from Approval_Advance_Pending__c - see the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Ticked automatically while this disposition has an approval awaiting a decision. It clears on approval, rejection or recall, and cannot be edited by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Approval Pending</label>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Checkbox</type>
</CustomField>
